== C. Symmetries of rho*(.,k) and the level floors ==
C1. the arena at level k depends only on q mod 2^(k-1): in arena(q + 2^(k-1)) node s has the options of node s + 2^(k-1) in arena(q) (odd s):
  [ok] k = 3..12, every odd q: option sets match (so G_sigma(q) and G_sigma'(q + 2^(k-1)) are isomorphic parity graphs with sigma'(s) = sigma(s + 2^(k-1)))
C2. rho*(q,k) = rho*(q + 2^(k-1),k) = rho*(-q,k) for every odd q mod 2^k, k = 3..10:
  [ok] both symmetries hold at k = 3..10 (all 2^(k-1) odd residues)
C3. the proof of rho*(-q,k) = rho*(q,k): the least fixed point f* of the Min operator at F = rho*(q,k) is nu-invariant, and (-sigma*, f*) certifies F for -q:
  [ok] 10 cases: nu-invariant f*, sigma* certify F for q; -sigma* with the same f* certifies F for -q (and the nu-symmetric Max certificate transports unchanged)
C4. strategy-level comparison at k = 4, 5 (pure-python Karp): the full rho_max distributions of q and -q can differ, the nu-invariant strategies (sigma(-s) = -sigma(s)) match under sigma -> -sigma:
  [ok] k = 4, 5: for every nu-invariant sigma of arena(q), rho_max(sigma) = rho_max(-sigma in arena(-q))
  [ok] k = 4: all-strategy distributions differ (q=3: [('1', 217), ('1/2', 8), ('2/3', 9)]..., q=5: [('1', 217), ('1/2', 4), ('2/3', 15)]...) but the minima agree (1/2)
C5. level floors min_q rho*(q,k) over the 2^(k-3) classes (+-q mod 2^(k-1)), k <= 11:
    k= 3: floor 1/2 (0.50000) attained by +-q mod 2^2 for q in [1] (1 of 1 classes); value spectrum [('1/2', 1)]...
    k= 4: floor 1/2 (0.50000) attained by +-q mod 2^3 for q in [1, 3] (2 of 2 classes); value spectrum [('1/2', 2)]...
    k= 5: floor 1/2 (0.50000) attained by +-q mod 2^4 for q in [1, 3, 5, 7] (4 of 4 classes); value spectrum [('1/2', 4)]...
    k= 6: floor 1/2 (0.50000) attained by +-q mod 2^5 for q in [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15] (8 of 8 classes); value spectrum [('1/2', 8)]...
    k= 7: floor 3/7 (0.42857) attained by +-q mod 2^6 for q in [5, 7, 9, 11] (4 of 16 classes); value spectrum [('3/7', 4), ('1/2', 12)]...
  [ok] k = 7: the classes with rho* = 3/7 are exactly +-5, +-7, +-9, +-11 mod 64 (all others 1/2): this is the q = 5..11 coincidence
    k= 8: floor 3/7 (0.42857) attained by +-q mod 2^7 for q in [5, 7, 9, 11, 53, 55, 57, 59] (8 of 32 classes); value spectrum [('3/7', 8), ('7/16', 1), ('4/9', 3), ('9/20', 1), ('5/11', 7), ('1/2', 12)]...
