== D. Theorem N: the negative-integer adversary; rho_max >= log_{q+1} 2 for every strategy of every q ==
D1. U_k (u -> u/2; u odd -> rho((qu -+ 1)/2) in [1, H]) is the Min graph of the arena when Max always takes the lift with top bit 1 (node N - u):
  [ok] k = 2..14, q = 3..65: edge sets coincide
D2. the multiplicative potential u: every odd step has 2 v <= (q+1) u, every even step v = u/2:
  [ok] k = 2..18, q = 3..65: all edges of U_k satisfy the potential inequalities (hence every cycle has (q+1)^a >= 2^p, density >= log_{q+1} 2)
D3. independent confirmation: least cycle density of U_k (numpy Karp) = value of the frozen strategy tau = 1 (game solver), and it is >= log_{q+1} 2:
  [ok] q = 3..21, k = 5..10: Karp(U_k) = frozen-tau value; all >= log_{q+1} 2
